ICES stomach-content datasets
-----------------------------
Objects: ices_diet, ices_stomachs, ices_lineage, ices_lineage_raw.

Observations are derived from a publicly downloadable ICES Stomach Content
Database extract (2020-2024; Greater North Sea ecoregion). The official ICES
Stomach Content Data inventory specifies Creative Commons Attribution 4.0
International (CC BY 4.0) for public data:
  https://stomachdata.ices.dk/inventory
  https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

Source attribution:
  ICES Stomach Content Database. ICES, Copenhagen.
  https://stomachdata.ices.dk/

The source extract was redistributed in the MIT-licensed stomachr software
project by Max Lindmark, from the public ICES API:
  https://github.com/maxlindmark/stomachr

Adaptations made for DietView include dropping empty-stomach placeholder prey
rows; joining prey, predator, haul and submission information; standardising
units; and deriving display columns. The ICES taxon keys were matched to a
WoRMS lineage from stomachr. For three unaccepted AphiaIDs the accepted
lineage is used in ices_lineage; the original lineage is also supplied.
Details and a reproducible script are in data-raw/ices_data.R (source repo).

The reporting organisations and source data providers retain their rights.
DietView does not imply endorsement by ICES. Always consult ICES's current
terms and any restrictions on specific data before redistributing additional
ICES records. Historic terms shipped with this extract are retained under
source-repository data-raw/ices/ICES_data_terms_Disclaimer.txt.

